{{IPA|/il ʔiʕˈlaːn il ʕaːˈlami li ħˈʔuːʔ il ʔinˈsaːn <nowiki>|</nowiki> il ˈband il ʔawwaˈlaːni/}}
<br />
{{IPA|/il bani ʔadˈmiːn kulˈluhum mawluˈdiːn ħurˈriːn wi mitsawˈjiːn fil kaˈrˤaːma wil ħuˈʔuːʔ <nowiki>||</nowiki> ʔetwahabˈlohom ilˈʕaʔle we ddˤaˈmiːr wel mafˈruːdˤ jeʕamlo baʕˈdˤiːhom biˈroːħ el ʔaxaˈwejja/}}
</blockquote>

IPA phonemic transcription (for a general demonstration of Egyptian phonology):
<blockquote>
{{IPA|/el ʔeʕˈlaːn el ʕaːˈlami le ħˈʔuːʔ el ʔenˈsaːn <nowiki>|</nowiki> el ˈband el ʔawwaˈlaːni/}}
<br />
{{IPA|/el bani ʔadˈmiːn kolˈlohom mawloˈdiːn ħorˈriːn we metsawˈjiːn fel kaˈrˤaːma wel ħoˈʔuːʔ <nowiki>||</nowiki> ʔetwahabˈlohom elˈʕaʔle we ddˤaˈmiːr wel mafˈruːdˤ jeˈʕamlu baʕˈdˤiːhom beˈroːħ el ʔaxaˈwejja/}}
</blockquote>

IPA phonetic transcription morphologically (in fast speech, [[vowel length|long vowels]] are half-long or without distinctive length):
<blockquote>
{{IPA|[el ʔeʕˈlæːn el ʕæˈlæmi le ħˈʔuːʔ el ʔenˈsæːn <nowiki>|</nowiki> el ˈbænd el ʔæwwæˈlæːni]}}
<br />
{{IPA|[el bæniʔædˈmiːn kolˈlohom mæwlʊˈdiːn ħʊrˈriːn we metsæwˈjiːn fel kɑˈɾɑːmɑ wel ħʊˈʔuːʔ <nowiki>||</nowiki> ʔetwæhæbˈlohom elˈʕæʔle we ddɑˈmiːɾ wel mɑfˈɾuːd jeˈʕæmlu bɑʕˈdiːhom beˈɾoːħ el ʔæxæˈwejjæ]}}
</blockquote>

'''English''':
<blockquote>
Article 1 of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights
<br />
All human beings are born free and equal in dignity and rights. They are endowed with reason and conscience and should act towards one another in the spirit of brotherhood.
</blockquote>

== Sample words and sentences ==
* {{lang|arz|إزيك}} {{IPA|[ezˈzæjjæk]}} ("How are you [m.]")
* {{lang|arz|إزيك}} {{IPA|[ezˈzæjjek]}} ("How are you [f.]")
* {{lang|arz|إزيكو}} {{IPA|[ezzæjˈjoko]}} ("How are you [pl.]")
* {{lang|arz|ايه ده}} {{IPA|[ˈʔeː ˈdæ]}} ("What is all this?", "What is the point", "What is this?" – expression of annoyance)
** Ex.: {{lang|arz|انت بتقوللهم عليا كده ليه, ايه ده؟}} {{IPA|[ˈentæ betʔolˈlohom ʕæˈlæjjæ ˈkedæ ˈleː ˈʔeː dæ]}} ("Why are you telling them such things about me, ''what is all this''?")
* {{lang|arz|خلاص}} {{IPA|[xɑˈlɑːsˤ]}}: several meanings, though its main meaning is "enough", often adverbial
** "Stop it!" Ex.: {{lang|arz|زهقت, خلاص}} {{IPA|[zeˈheʔte xɑˈlɑːsˤ]}} ("I'm annoyed, ''stop it!''")
** "It is over!", "finally, eventually" {{lang|arz|مامتى كانت عيانه و ماتت, خلاص}}  Ex.: {{IPA|[ˈmɑmti kæːnet ʕajˈjæːnæ wˈmæːtet xɑˈlɑːsˤ]}}| ("My mother was ill and died ''finally''." [or "...and'' it is over now''"])
** "Ok, then!" Ex.: {{lang|arz|خلاص, أشوفك بكرا}} {{IPA|[xɑˈlɑːsˤ ʔæˈʃuːfæk ˈbokɾɑ]}} ("I'll see you tomorrow ''then''")
* {{lang|arz|خالص}} {{IPA|[ˈxɑːlesˤ]}} ("at all")
** {{lang|arz|ماعندناش حاجه نقولها خالص}} {{IPA|[mæʕændeˈnæːʃ ˈħæːɡæ nˈʔolhæ ˈxɑːlesˤ]}} ("We have nothing ''at all'' to say")
* {{lang|arz|كفاية}} {{IPA|[keˈfæːjæ]}} ("It is enough!" or "That is enough")
* {{lang|arz|يعنى}} {{IPA|[ˈjæʕni]}} ("that is to say" or "meaning" or "y'know")
** As answer to {{lang|arz|انت عامل إيه؟}} {{IPA|[entæ ˈʕæːmel ˈ(ʔ)eː]}} ("How do you do [m.]?") (as an answer: {{lang|arz|مش أد كده}} {{IPA|[meʃ ˈʔædde ˈkedæ]}} "I am so so" or {{lang|arz|نص نص}} {{IPA|[ˈnosˤse ˈnosˤ]}} {{lit|"half half"}} = {{lang|arz|مش تمام}} {{IPA|[meʃ tæˈmæːm]}} "not perfect")
** {{lang|arz|يعنى ايه؟}} {{IPA|[jæʕni ˈʔeː]}} ("What does that ''mean?''")
** {{lang|arz|امتى هتخلص يعنى؟}} {{IPA|[ˈemtæ hɑtˈxɑllɑsˤ ˈjæʕni]}} ("When are you finishing ''exactly, then''?)
* {{lang|arz|بقى}} {{IPA|[ˈbæʔæ]}} (particle of enforcement → "just" in imperative clauses and "well,...then?" in questions)
** {{lang|arz|هاته بقى}} {{IPA|[ˈhæːto ˈbæʔæ]}} ("''Just'' give it to me!)" {{lang|arz|عمل ايه بقى؟}} {{IPA|[ˈʕæmæl ˈ(ʔ)eː ˈbæʔæ]}} ''or''&nbsp; {{IPA|[ˈʕæmæl ˈ(ʔ)eː ˈbæʔæ]}} ("''Well'', what did he do ''then''?")

